The quieting experiment exposes the key obstruction. If the planted rows retain any efficiently detectable balance/correlation structure, a standard exact search recovers them; if those signatures are removed, the paper supplies no compact route for a no-tool solver—the task becomes pure subset enumeration. The theorem’s lower bound does not transfer to the inverse-planted distribution. I’m documenting this as a two-track rejection rather than shipping an unsupported Track A claim or an artificial Track B puzzle.
