The natural planted VC-dimension family clears G and V but fails H:

- Track A: the paper proves worst-case rETH hardness via Label Cover, not hardness for inverse-planted matrices.
- A structure-aware balance search recovered prototype witnesses in 0.064–0.069 seconds.
- Track B: no shorter paper-derived route exists; the same search requires roughly 321k–343k trace updates, while even checking one guessed witness takes 2,048 inspections—over the 300-operation cap.
- Littlestone witnesses are full binary mistake trees and exceed the 256-atom cap before reaching the theorem’s hardness regime.

The complete evidence and theorem references are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/REJECTED.md). The source paper is available from [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.09517).
