new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e5ca8c7106cd223783536b1f864a4e8104fd00f2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+# VC-shattering generator for arXiv:1705.09517
+
+Status: **locally verified Track B candidate; not yet shippable**.  The required
+four-vendor run is blocked by OpenRouter HTTP 403 (`Key limit exceeded (total
+limit)`), so no oracle failure is being claimed.
+
+| profile field | value |
+|---|---|
+| track | B — an efficient algorithm is disclosed |
+| native domain | combinatorics |
+| object regime | finite discrete |
+| computational core | other (fixed-size shattered-subset search) |
+| certificate | integer tuple (a subset of universe indices) |
+| intuition | symmetry: a common symmetric-difference mask between two concept halves |
+| domain essentiality | native |
+| reduction | none |
+
+## Problem and trust boundary
+
+The family uses the native object in Manurangsi and Rubinstein,
+[*Inapproximability of VC Dimension and Littlestone's Dimension*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.09517):
+an explicit Boolean incidence matrix for a finite concept class.  The solver must
+give exactly `k` universe elements.  `verify` projects every concept onto those
+elements and checks that all `2^k` binary patterns occur, exactly the shattering
+definition in Section 2 (Definition 3 in the paper's numbering).  It accepts any
+valid shattered subset and never reads the planted answer.
+
+Generation is inverse, not search.  Rows indexed internally by `(x,t)` show every
+labelling `x` twice on the planted coordinates.  Decoy coordinates are a randomly
+disguised, low-dimensional Walsh family and flip with `t`; row and column labels are
+randomized.  Consequently the planted coordinates are shattered by construction.
+Every column has the same degree and every pair has the same exact 2-by-2 table.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+Theorem 1 is a worst-case rETH inapproximability result, and Theorem 13 obtains its
+gap from a particular Label-Cover reduction.  Neither result gives distributional
+hardness for this inverse-planted family, so Track A would be false.  Section 1 also
+states the general exact algorithm: enumerate element tuples up to
+`log2(|C|)`, taking `|U|^{O(log |C|)}` time.
+
+For this distribution, the disclosed reference algorithm counts row-pair XORs and
+tests a translation stabilizer.  At the hard preset it succeeds on 8/8 seeds,
+averaging 524,860 XOR/hash operations and 4.13 seconds.  The candidate language has
+14,783,142,660 subsets.  Once the aligned-half symmetry is noticed, comparing one
+corresponding row pair and reading the zero positions takes 120 bit operations.
+That mechanical-versus-compact gap is the Track B claim; it is not a claim that the
+paper's hard Label-Cover instances contain this symmetry.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+For `make_instance(n=7, witness_size=3, decoy_rank=2, seed=5)`, the complete concept
+matrix is:
+
+```text
+0000: 1100101
+0001: 0100011
+0002: 0001111
+0003: 1001000
+0004: 0000110
+0005: 1001001
+0006: 1100010
+0007: 0101100
+0008: 1010011
+0009: 0010101
+0010: 0111001
+0011: 1111110
+0012: 0110000
+0013: 1111111
+0014: 1010100
+0015: 0011010
+```
+
+The answer is `[0, 3, 6]` and `verify(inst, [0, 3, 6])` returns `(True, "ok")`.
+Dropping one element gives `verify(inst, [0, 3]) == (False, "wrong length: expected
+3 indices, got 2")`.  A person can solve this demo on paper by tabulating the eight
+three-bit projections; in fact all 35 three-subsets happen to be valid at this
+illustrative rung.
+
+## Presets
+
+| preset | `|U|` | `k` | concepts | candidate subsets | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 7 | 3 | 16 | 35 | hand example; never ships |
+| easy | 8 | 4 | 32 | 70 | awaits oracle ladder |
+| medium | 10 | 5 | 64 | 252 | awaits oracle ladder |
+| hard | 60 | 9 | 1,024 | 14,783,142,660 | provisional shipping preset |
+
+## Local gates
+
+| gate | measured result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 12/12 planted cases verify; answers JSON-round-trip |
+| G2 | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reason classes |
+| G3 | tagged prose/fenced answer round-trips |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 structure-aware uniform subset guesses; 98.50 s |
+| G5 | shipping density estimate 0/200,000; demo exact 35/35; baseline 524,860 operations / 4.81 s |
+| G6 | degree, greedy, 256-restart, pairwise-correlation, and adjacent-row attacks: each 0/8; reference 8/8 |
+| G7 | `n=120` builds and verifies with the same nine-element answer length |
+| G8 | 60/60 relabelling checks, 60/60 carried-witness checks, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | 35 characters, about 9 tokens, 9 atoms; intended route 120 operations |
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
+
+The required bare run made four retry calls at `easy`; all returned HTTP 403 before
+producing a reply.  The harness correctly recorded each as `solved="error"` and
+aborted rather than manufacturing hardness from an API failure.
+
+| arm | solved / attempts | result |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0 / 0 valid attempts | blocked by account quota |
+| structural hint | 0 / 0 | not run |
+| placebo hint | 0 / 0 | not run |
+
+`hinted - placebo` is therefore undefined, not zero.  The structural hint names
+only the common symmetric-difference mask; it does not state the resulting subset
+or chain an algorithm.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_1705_09517 import make_instance, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(n=60, witness_size=9, decoy_rank=6, seed=123)
+ok, reason = verify(inst, inst["answer"])
+assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After valid oracle evidence exists, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1705.09517 20 hard
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- The aligned halves are generator-added Track B structure and are
+  presentation-sensitive.  Reordering concepts preserves the mathematical set
+  system and the witness but removes the 120-operation shortcut; the slower
+  translation-stabilizer scan still works on the unordered row set.
+- `0/200,000` is an observed density under uniform sampling of canonical `k`-subsets,
+  not a proof that the true probability is zero and not a claim about a solver's
+  nonuniform prior.
+- The five attacks deliberately cover unary, pairwise, greedy, restart, and a wrong
+  local symmetry guess.  No SAT/SMT encoding, GPU search, or full
+  `|U|^{O(log |C|)}` enumeration was run.  The successful stabilizer algorithm is
+  disclosed separately, as Track B requires.
+- `canonical_key` is the multiset of exact three-column projection histograms.  It
+  is invariant under row and column permutations and separated all tested seeds,
+  but it is a strong cheap invariant, not a complete incidence-isomorphism canonizer.
+- Most importantly, the mandatory multi-vendor hardening and both G9 comparison
+  arms remain missing.  Do not treat this directory as a shipped hardness result
+  until those script-owned transcripts exist and the self-test is rerun with their
+  measured counts.
