codex
Implemented a native Track B VC-shattering generator based on the paper’s explicit concept-class definition and quasi-polynomial enumeration result ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.09517)).

Local verification is complete:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference scan: 524,860 operations, 8/8 solved.
- Compact symmetry route: 120 operations, 8/8 solved.
- Canonical-key checks: 140/140 invariance and witness checks.
- Maximum answer: 36 characters, 9 elements.

Deliverables:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/gen_1705_09517.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1705.09517/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet shippable: every required OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` before an oracle answered. The transcripts correctly record errors rather than false model failures. Restore the OpenRouter quota and rerun the bare and two isolated G9 hardening runs; no generator changes are otherwise required.
